# The keychain (Secret Service) that holds the sign-in, and System Settings for the accounts page
Recommends: kwallet6 | gnome-keyring,
            systemsettings
Description: Account service and shared core of the Microsoft 365 apps for KDE Plasma
 The sign-in shared by Graph Sync, Graph Mail and the other apps of the suite:
 the account service graphaccountsd (D-Bus activated) keeps one sign-in per
 account in the system keychain and hands out access tokens to the suite's
 programs; System Settings > Microsoft 365 Accounts lists the accounts, adds
 one, signs in again and signs out. Not affiliated with Microsoft.

Package: libgraphcore0.14
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: plasma-graphcore-linux
Description: Microsoft Graph library of the Microsoft 365 apps for KDE Plasma
 The library the suite's apps share: accounts, the client of the account
 service, a Microsoft Graph client with throttling and retries, the system's
 proxy settings, error messages, people search and the update check.
 .
 Named after its release series: series 0.14 can be installed next to others.

